 "notes": "All 10 planned old kinds kept; Viognier and Muscat added (Wikipedia-sourced). Archetypes are appellations/regional styles (maker-free, mk empty). Old models moved into archetype versions only where a retrieved page or the model's own name ties them to the archetype; the rest stay in m. Dropped: retailer own-label 'Villa Maria Tesco Finest Black Birch', and unknown-origin SKUs 'Delta Sauvignon Blanc', 'Grand Napa Vineyards Sauvignon Blanc', 'Emma Marris Chardonnay', 'House of Cards Ace High Chardonnay', 'Sidewood Mappinga Chardonnay' (second Sidewood SKU). Old unattributed grand cru names (Montrachet family, Corton-Charlemagne, Charlemagne, Chablis Grand Cru) became archetypes/versions. Not added for lack of a retrieved source: Puligny-/Chassagne-Montrachet village archetypes, Margaret River Chardonnay, Pfalz/Nahe Riesling, Weinviertel DAC year, producer names for Pouilly-Fumé and Wachau. No traditions (appellations are not craft traditions)."
